From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:56:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] DriveSetup: lock the window while scanning the disks in
 Run()

Since "DriveSetup: Register anyboot disk images in RefsReceived()."
(08afac4cda), MainWindow::Run() starts the window's thread and then
scans the disks, adding the rows of the partition list. Show() calls
Run() without the window's lock, so adding a row could drop into the
debugger with "Looper must be locked." (BView::CopyBits() from
OutlineView::AddRow()), as it did in the LUKS2 UI test, which has four
disks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/apps/drivesetup/MainWindow.cpp | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/apps/drivesetup/MainWindow.cpp b/src/apps/drivesetup/MainWindow.cpp
index 37e538f229..41890f028b 100644
--- a/src/apps/drivesetup/MainWindow.cpp
+++ b/src/apps/drivesetup/MainWindow.cpp
@@ -411,8 +411,12 @@ MainWindow::Run()
 			strerror(result));
 	}
 
-	// visit all disks in the system and show their contents
-	_ScanDrives();
+	// visit all disks in the system and show their contents (the window's
+	// thread runs already, and Show() calls Run() without the window's lock)
+	if (Lock()) {
+		_ScanDrives();
+		Unlock();
+	}
 
 	// If DeskBar isn't running, DriveSetup was probably started from Installer.
 	// Make sure to show on all workspaces, so the window doesn't disappear when using the
